#kaocha/v1
;; :kaocha.hooks/post-load ARMS malli `m/=>` instrumentation for the whole run.
;;
;; post-load, not pre-run and not pre-load: `m/=>` registers at LOAD time and
;; `instrument!` only covers what is registered when it is called, so arming
;; before the namespaces load silently instruments nothing while printing exactly
;; what success prints. lvgl-codegen.instrument/arm! carries the argument, the
;; non-vacuity floor and the proof that vars were measurably replaced;
;; lvgl-codegen.instrument-test is its canary and names what to revert to break it.
{:tests [{:id :unit :source-paths ["src"] :test-paths ["test"]}]
 ;; The hooks PLUGIN is what reads :kaocha.hooks/* — without it the key is
 ;; inert config and the seam never fires, which the canary caught.
 :plugins [:kaocha.plugin/hooks]
 ;; spec-coverage is NOT a hook here: `:kaocha.hooks/post-run` was measured NOT TO
 ;; FIRE (a namespace enrolled at 0% left the suite green), so it drives its own run
 ;; via `clojure -M:spec-coverage`. post-load works, which is why arming still uses it.
 :kaocha.hooks/post-load [lvgl-codegen.instrument/arm!]}
